recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the lap closed clean and the standing question sharpened rather than moved. A guard's reach has now been the finding three times in one day, each time caught by a hand rather than by a meter, and each time the numbers were already printed. The next honest instrument is a reading that compares what a guard COUNTS against what its box HOLDS and reports the difference by name -- one number, every guard, so a narrow filter announces itself instead of waiting for a hand to trip over it. That is a real design and it wants your word before it becomes a fleet-wide meter. Also still yours, unchanged: 82 of 607 reachable living pages lead nowhere and a ceiling with no floor scores each at 100.
